  "notes": "{捕手|ほしゅ} is the formal Japanese baseball term for catcher ({捕|ほ} = catch + {手|しゅ} = player). In casual conversation, キャッチャー (from English) is equally common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {正捕手|せいほしゅ}: starting/regular catcher\n- {控|ひか}え{捕手|ほしゅ}: backup catcher\n- {捕手|ほしゅ}を{務|つと}める: to serve as catcher\n\nRELATED POSITIONS:\n- {投手|とうしゅ}: pitcher\n- {内野手|ないやしゅ}: infielder\n- {外野手|がいやしゅ}: outfielder\n- {打者|だしゃ}: batter\n\nUSAGE:\nThe {投手|とうしゅ} and {捕手|ほしゅ} together form the バッテリー (battery). Newspapers and sports broadcasts prefer the kanji term {捕手|ほしゅ}, while spoken language often uses キャッチャー.",
